{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1393842-a-2e-city","id":1393842,"title":"A 2E City","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-03T13:32:36-07:00","id":1393842,"title":"A 2E City","content":"So with all this time, I'm populating LA with monsters. So this thread is about prometheans. Do prometheans have a society in a city? I know that their wasteland prevents too many from living in a city at once? Do ones of the same refinement get together? What kinds on numbers could LA hold, especially with other splats also populating the city.? I'm going to re read the promethean book again to get a feel for it, but I think that this community can make it easier to figure it all out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T19:06:55-07:00","id":1393899,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, I was wondering when this would reach here. I've run Promethean before, and I'll do it again, so hopefully I can help!<br /> The short answer is: Promethean is weird, and the book can't really give you satisfying answers to these questions, because the answers are based on individuals in a way that isn't true for Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, or most other games. But I would guess, that, assuming no weirdness, the closest &quot;canon&quot; answers you'd get to your questions are, respectively:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do prometheans have a society in a city? </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that their wasteland prevents too many from living in a city at once? </div> </div> </div>Not technically, but makes it practically difficult when they happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do ones of the same refinement get together? </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, but probably not in any political way. It might also suggest an underlying problem with the group or misunderstanding on their part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What kinds on numbers could LA hold, especially with other splats also populating the city.? </div> </div> </div>L.A. could hold every Promethean on the planet, but realistically there will be, at most, 3 to 5 of them there at time.<br /> <br /> But none of those are really satisfying without context. So, have some of that; hopefully it explains my answers well enough?<br /> <br /> To start, the corebook claims that, &quot;At any given time, there might be one hundred Created walking the Earth.&quot; So, unless something <i>unusual</i> is going on, there are unlikely to be more than a handful of Created anywhere. At all. This means you don't really get the political organizations or faiths that you find in other gamelines. Promethean existence is too transient and personal for it. As a result, Prometheans are often solitary, and their experience of other Created is in a hazy, collective memory, or through the artifacts and messages others leave behind.<br /> The 2e Night Horrors book <i>kinda</i> contradicts this, but it's also a toolbox for a toolbox, and would probably leave the global Promethean population hovering somewhere between 150 to 200, anyway.<br /> <br /> Transience kinda permeates the Promethean condition, and so they don't usually stick in one place for too long. In 2e this isn't so much the fault of an inevitable blighting of the land, but a consequence of the Pilgrimage itself. They have to go and experience new things, meet new friends, make new enemies, and be new people. If they don't regularly make progress, they risk sabotaging their Great Work or festering a Wasteland [or both]. Every Created has a path she must walk, and she'll usually find she literally walks it, stepping forward and backward alongside the milestones of her Pilgrimage!<br /> <br /> Which brings me to Refinements, which are the means by which a Promethean makes the bulk of their journey. A Promethean isn't just expected to adopt multiple Refinements over the course of their Pilgrimage, they have to! If they want to be human, they have to sample the breadth of what makes humanity human. The Refinements, and the Roles within them, help them do that. Promethean is a game of constant motion. While individuals can get stuck in a Role, whether due to comfort or lack of understanding, their very nature pushes them to understand, internalize, and move on.<br /> <br /> Now, none of this means that a Promethean can't spend their entire existence in a single city, just that the vast majority will eventually move on. There are so many things driving them to keep moving, whether it is the hope of a New Dawn, the failure of Wasteland, or mobs of Disquieted mortals. Angels interfere with their lives, drawing them towards the paths they must [or mustn't] follow. Sometimes, they find others, and build a throng. Those Created are usually [but not always] player characters.<br /> <br /> All of that said, Promethean is also a game of broken rules. Despite their rarity, Prometheans will still encounter each other, even when it seems contrived. As the Divine Fire conspires to entangle them, a whole lot of Created can find their paths intersecting, only to later find it was necessary for their growth. So if you <i>want</i> more of them than a handful, you can have as many as you like. Though, at some point, you might need to figure out why so many have been drawn here, and what designs the Principle might have for them. Or maybe treat it like a mystery in Mage, I dunno?<br /> <br /> In addition, sometimes a Promethean steps off the Pilgrimage entirely, adopting the Refinement of Flux. These Created embrace their monsterhood and abandon the quest for humanity. They are excellent options if you want more sedentary Created, as they can more easily make lairs and don't usually care about their effects on humanity. As well, if you want to maybe compensate for a relative lack of Created, some of their antagonists can fill in for them. Guilds of alchemists can operate similarly to some of the secret societies of other games, and even offer more explicit crossover opportunities with the likes of Hunter or Deviant.<br /> <br /> Anyway, hope this helps? Or at least offers you a stronger starting point? Hopefully it isn't too rambley!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T19:48:53-07:00","id":1393917,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: what do you call it when a group of Prometheans get together and trade stories? A Ramble. So being rambly is appropriate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The extent of organization in Promethean \u201csociety\u201d is the Throng: a handful of Prometheans who have been drawn together by the Divine Fire. You're more likely to see, say, five Prometheans traveling together than a lone Promethean. <br /> <br /> Another aspect of Promethean \u201csociety\u201d to consider is the Athanors. These are objects (though frequently not portable) that serve various functions for the Prometheans that find them, such as Pilgrimage Markers and Sanctuaries (and a number of less savory functions). They can be a reason for Prometheans to visit a place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T21:33:35-07:00","id":1393938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1393842-a-2e-city?p=1393917#post1393917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another aspect of Promethean \u201csociety\u201d to consider is the Athanors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Azothic Memory in general. Anyone who's ever followed the Refinement of Lead could theoretically have retained the Plumb the Fathoms Alembic, which opens up a lot of options for steering Prometheans toward things relevant to their experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T16:03:14-07:00","id":1394177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1393842-a-2e-city?p=1393917#post1393917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The extent of organization in Promethean \u201csociety\u201d is the Throng: a handful of Prometheans who have been drawn together by the Divine Fire. You're more likely to see, say, five Prometheans traveling together than a lone Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a far more succinct way of putting it than anything I said.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I find it interesting how the Promethean book says one thing about Prometheans [they're solitary, can spend decades without seeing another of their kind, etc], but shows the reader something else entirely. Because, thinking about it, most example characters in the books are in one or more throngs, and an entire Refinement's signature Transmutation is <i>reliant</i> on membership in a branded throng. Any Promethean whose journey includes Aes has to meet and make nice with other Created, and, between Elpis and <i>qashmallim</i>, it definitely feels like solitary wanderers should be the exception, rather than the rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another aspect of Promethean \u201csociety\u201d to consider is the Athanors. </div> </div> </div>This is actually probably the best way to explain any sustained Created presence in L.A., especially paired with Satchel's advice. A cluster of unusual or potent Pilgrimage Markers [or even one left by the Seer herself] could potentially inspire one or more Created to linger and protect them. Or maybe there's an Athanor buried somewhere in the city with unusual effects? I seem to recall the Great Pyramid being an Athanor that quelled Disquiet around it at the cost of preventing all Pandorans within its radiance from going dormant, but cannot find it anywhere. Maybe I made it up?<br /> <br /> Anyway, make a throng, maybe make two. Give them a reason to stick around. Sprinkle a Centimanus, or a handful, into the surrounding area and add any alchemist guilds or other antagonists to taste. You'll be moving on to Changeling in no time!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nitpick: what do you call it when a group of Prometheans get together and trade stories? A Ramble. So being rambly is appropriate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Ha, I guess you're right!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T16:17:46-07:00","id":1394179,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it takes a bit to make forty mages.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1393842-a-2e-city?p=1393899#post1393899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, have some of that; hopefully it explains my answers well enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, that was a great explanation.<br /> <br /> I'll take this all into consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}